 ## Pre-training data hygiene
-- SHA-256 + pHash (Hamming ≤ 8) dedup.
-- DINOv2 ViT-B/14 embeddings → drop > 2σ from class centroid.
-- Cleanlab label-issue ranking + FiftyOne embedding browser to triage
-  top-N suspects.
-- Manual validation pass: 200–300 photos per class.
-- Hierarchical sidecar metadata per crop: `plant_id`, `species`,
-  `diagnosis`, `severity`, `leaf_or_whole_plant`, `capture_session`,
-  `source`, `label_confidence`, `bbox`. Splits are disjoint by
-  `plant_id` (never let the same plant appear in train and val).
-
-## Time budget on 1× A100-40
-- 5–10 min DINOv2-S frozen + linear probe (mandatory diagnostic)
-- ~35 min EfficientNetV2-S fine-tune (teacher)
-- 10–15 min KD into MobileNetV3-Large student
-- 5 min temperature calibration + ONNX export
+
+* Per-class SHA-256 + pHash dedup (Hamming ≤ 6) on `TRAIN_ROOT` only.
+  Cross-class similarities are kept on purpose — they help as hard
+  negatives during KD.
+* Sidecar JSON per crop: `plant_id`, `species`, `diagnosis`, `severity`,
+  `leaf_or_whole_plant`, `capture_session`, `source`, `label_confidence`,
+  `bbox`. Group splits use `(source, plant_id)` so the same plant
+  never appears in both `TRAIN_ROOT` and a held-out split.
+* Exact SHA-256 leakage audit between `TRAIN_ROOT` and every held-out
+  split — `RuntimeError` on overlap.
+* `ImageFolder.target_transform` remap on every eval loader, so a
+  slice that is missing one trained class cannot silently shift
+  labels.
+
+## Time budget on 1× A100-40 (rough)
+
+| Phase | Time |
+|---|---|
+| §2 data fetch (cold cache) | 8–15 min |
+| §3 dedup + DINOv2-S probe | 5–10 min |
+| §4 EfficientNetV2-S fine-tune | 25–35 min |
+| §5 KD into MobileNetV3-Large | 8–12 min |
+| §6 ONNX + INT8 + temperature + conformal | 5 min |
+
+Colab T4 is roughly 2-3× slower; reduce `BATCH=64`.
 
 ## Known caveats
-- `viral_disease` is incurable; the pipeline auto-escalates severity
-  by one level on any high-confidence viral verdict.
-- `edema` and `nutrient_deficiency` are physiological / nutritional —
-  neither is an infection. They were added to give the AI Doctor
-  honest options for the most common indoor mis-diagnoses.
+
+* `viral_disease` is incurable; the server pipeline auto-escalates
+  severity by one level on any high-confidence viral verdict.
